'''amethystine''' (am-ẹ̄-this′tin), ''a.'' [< L. ''amethystinus'', < Gr. ἀμεθύστινος, < ἀμέθυστος, amethyst: see ''amethyst''.] '''1.''' Pertaining to or resembling amethyst; of the color of amethyst; purple; violet. {{smaller|Anciently applied to a garment of the color of amethyst, as distinguished from the Tyrian and hyacinthine purple.}}
{{smaller block|<poem>Trembling water-drops,
That glimmer with an ''amethystine'' light.</poem>
{{right|''Bryant'', Winter Piece.}}}}
'''2.''' Composed of amethyst: as, an ''amethystine'' cup.

